{"id":"86189377faa0d250d2cb1b7cccf656fe50cc7032a95e4ff7881edc61fc551d6a","at":"2026-10-27T06:35:25Z","commit":"7705590ec4f2b89554527d01b131dbbb10f2280e","parents":["4214015469c2d49b31693dcee48e97b9b6e8e71fe7493a7bd00594cca0f4ca3d"],"op":"relate","type":"verifies","ends":[{"kind":"test","id":"Macaw.Auth.PlugTest: require_role without fetch_flash still goes home, without a message","hash":"93fbd159"},{"kind":"spec","id":"spec/02-plugs.md#plug-require-role-no-flash","hash":"3e59a7e3"}],"by":"Doug ClymerOlson <doug@yarina.org>","note":"Reviewed after #88 narrowed the hint to the signed-in case (the signed-out clause moved to plug-require-role-signed-out, since a signed-out request now goes to sign in): a signed-in viewer through require_role([\"admin\"]) without fetch_flash; assert halted and location /home checks 'still sent home', refute Map.has_key?(assigns, :flash) checks 'no :flash is assigned'. The removed signed-out assertion is now checked, inverted, by the signed-out tests.","basis":"review"}
{"id":"fb3b3febc1037e3c54a3088568dd810e8e07cebaa4f633982804fc7a4c7461d9","at":"2026-10-27T06:35:30Z","commit":"7705590ec4f2b89554527d01b131dbbb10f2280e","parents":["b69c30ef7ae35dacc2029f4f6ebb51f67336384cc6e7b8588942964f5a401667"],"op":"relate","type":"verifies","ends":[{"kind":"test","id":"Macaw.Auth.PlugTest: require_role still sends a signed-in user without the role home, remembering nothing","hash":"ccad9632"},{"kind":"spec","id":"spec/02-plugs.md#plug-require-role-signed-in","hash":"bd4aa1c9"}],"by":"Doug ClymerOlson <doug@yarina.org>","note":"Reviewed: the test pins behavior #88 keeps, so it could not go red; it passed against both require_role versions. A signed-in viewer's GET to /admin through require_role([\"admin\"]) after fetch_flash: assert halted and status 302 and location /home checks 'halted with 302 to home'; Phoenix.Flash.get(:error) == 'You are not allowed to do that.' checks the error flash; get_session(macaw_auth_return_to) == nil checks 'no return path is remembered', the line the signed-out branch's remember_return must not reach.","basis":"review"}
{"id":"93486345a816414eccba5978efb5709e2f37de033cfa739b24a07f81ba249c7b","at":"2026-10-27T06:35:37Z","commit":"7705590ec4f2b89554527d01b131dbbb10f2280e","parents":["b9cd9eb2820dd200e8a417162dcbceabf6d47c3b9bb8e9b2afbe46c31b343a74"],"op":"relate","type":"verifies","ends":[{"kind":"test","id":"Macaw.Auth.PlugTest: the sections of spec 02: authorize's options, its resource only when signed in, and a step it leaves alone","hash":"0721ac44"},{"kind":"spec","id":"spec/02-plugs.md#auth-plug-authorize","hash":"dabcf9de"}],"by":"Doug ClymerOlson <doug@yarina.org>","note":"Judgement: #88 reworded only §4.1's signed-out bullet, dropping 'Unlike require_role/2, which sends a signed-out request home' for 'as require_authenticated/2 and require_role/2 do'. authorize/2's own behavior (sign in, GET remembered) is unchanged and its code untouched; the require_role half of the comparison is §4's claim, verified by plug-require-role-signed-out and the §4 section test.","basis":"judgement"}
{"id":"c701a11966466a5915dcefdc74c77495f6e5c8ed7929b2d1cbc71ccfdd392433","at":"2026-10-27T06:35:58Z","commit":"7705590ec4f2b89554527d01b131dbbb10f2280e","parents":["b78dfc027844046d76f3a224678159c816daa7295e92fd07d48fcf290d5cf4dc"],"op":"relate","type":"tests","ends":[{"kind":"test","id":"Macaw.Auth.PlugTest: require_role still sends a signed-in user without the role home, remembering nothing","hash":"ccad9632"},{"kind":"code","id":"Macaw.Auth.Plug.require_role/2","hash":"beeed5b5"}],"by":"Doug ClymerOlson <doug@yarina.org>","note":"Structural: both tests still call require_role/2 directly after #88 changed its signed-out branch; each passed against the new version (green run) as it did against the old."}
